<title>USA: Fannie Mae to redeem $864.2 mln in notes.</title>
<headline>Fannie Mae to redeem $864.2 mln in notes.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fannie Mae on Monday said it will redeem all outstanding amounts of one debenture issue totalling $500 million and four medium-term note issues totalling $364.2 million as follows.</p>
<p>The terms of the debenture, which has series number</p>
<p>SM-2002-G, are as follows.</p>
<p>  Principal     Interest    Maturity    Cusip     Redemption</p>
<p>   Amount	   Rate	  Date	Number	Date</p>
<p> $500 million     7.30	07/10/02   3135865J4   07/16/97</p>
<p>The terms of the medium-term notes are as follows.</p>
<p>  Principal     Interest    Maturity    Cusip     Redemption</p>
<p>   Amount	   Rate	  Date	Number	Date</p>
<p> $100 million     6.50	06/26/98   31364CFK9   06/26/97</p>
<p> $100 million     6.92	06/02/00   31364BDE7   07/16/97</p>
<p>  $89.2 million   6.95	05/23/00   31364BDC1   07/16/97</p>
<p>  $75 million     7.10	06/04/01   31364CDU9   06/26/97</p>
<p>The redemption price of the issues will be 100 percent of the principal amount plus interest accrued to the redemption date, Fannie Mae said.</p>
</text>
